const body = `<h1>9.4c — Combat Abilities Engine: Interface-Driven Combat</h1>

<div class="callout warn">
    <strong>Season 2: beyond the exam.</strong> This topic is no longer tested
    (the 2025 CED removed inheritance from the exam). We build it after May 12
    because it makes the RPG engine dramatically better, and because you are
    ready for it. Pure craft, zero test anxiety.
</div>



<div class="activity expand-app">
    <div class="activity-header">
        <span class="activity-label">Expand Application</span>
        <span class="activity-time">~30 min</span>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h3>Build: Ability System</h3>
        <p>Professional RPGs use an interface for all combat actions. "Attack", "Heal", "Fireball", "Shield Block" — they all conform to the same contract. This lets you build an ability bar that works with anything.</p>
        <p>Create interface <code>CombatAction</code>:</p>
        <ol>
            <li><code>String getName()</code></li>
            <li><code>int getPower()</code></li>
            <li><code>String getTargetType()</code> — returns "enemy", "ally", or "self"</li>
            <li><code>String execute()</code> — returns a description of what happened</li>
        </ol>
        <p>Create at least 4 implementations:</p>
        <ol>
            <li><code>Slash</code>: power=12, target=enemy</li>
            <li><code>Fireball</code>: power=25, target=enemy</li>
            <li><code>HealingLight</code>: power=15, target=ally</li>
            <li><code>DefensiveStance</code>: power=0, target=self — execute() returns "Defense doubled for 2 turns!"</li>
        </ol>
        <p>Store all 4 in a <code>CombatAction[]</code> array. Print each action's name, power, target, and execution result.</p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="resources">
    <h3>Reference Docs</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-09/object-interfaces-casting.html">Interfaces</a></li>
        <li><a href="../docs/unit-09/extends-and-super.html">Inheritance</a></li>
    </ul>
</div>`;
